# [Perf] [AMD] Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: Pack the FP8 GDN input projections on ROCm
# https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/50024  (PR head f88569cd120660801e00459449856f1f1e0a844a, a merge of main; the diff below is the PR's own changes)
# Generated against the SGLang checkout of the image (1ced9a9eb0) with patches 01-08 applied; source files only (tests dropped).
# One FP8 quant and one GEMM for the GDN in_proj_qkvz and in_proj_ba of up to 64 rows (decode and verify
# steps), instead of two of each. It is on by default; SGLANG_QWEN35_PACKED_IN_PROJ=0 turns it off. The monokernel
# points (c1 TP1/2/4, c2) set it to 0: the monokernel covers the steps this packs, and packing builds a second
# copy of the projections (about 1.5 GB) that those points do not read.

diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/models/qwen3_5.py b/python/sglang/srt/models/qwen3_5.py
